<title>NETHERLANDS: WORLD COURT TO HEAR HUNGARY-SLOVAKIA DAM DISPUTE.</title>
<headline>WORLD COURT TO HEAR HUNGARY-SLOVAKIA DAM DISPUTE.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Court of Justice said on Thursday it would open hearings on March 3 in a dispute between Hungary and Slovakia over the latter's diversion of the Danube's waters for a hydroelectric power project.</p>
<p>Slovakia unilaterally diverted a long stretch of the Danube in 1992 to build the Gabcikovo dam after Hungary withdrew from a joint agreement for a similar dam at Nagymaros in Hungary.</p>
<p>Slovakia alleges Hungary breached contractual obligations while the Hungarians say diverting the river, which forms the border between the two countries, breaks international law and has caused widespread ecological damage.</p>
<p>The International Court of Justice is the main judicial organ of the United Nations and settles disputes between states in accordance with international law.  201655 GMT feb 97</p>
</text>
